      "id": "ML-C100-mundu",
      "sequence": 3570,
      "title": "മുണ്ട് (muṇṭŭ) — a mundu",
      "headword": "മുണ്ട്",
      "romanization": "muṇṭŭ",
      "gloss": "a mundu — the first garment the book names, after teaching the cloth it is made of",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:b33a50c00235c9e4",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say the word for cloth. Then say new."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മുണ്ട് — muṇṭŭ — a mundu, the length of cloth worn wrapped at the waist."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇത് പുതിയ മുണ്ടാണ്. — itŭ putiya muṇṭāṇŭ — \"This is a new mundu.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The book gave you the cloth before it gave you the garment. തുണി is the stuff; മുണ്ട് (muṇṭŭ) is the thing made of it and worn."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two things in that sentence you already know how to do, and neither is new:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പുതിയ sits in front and does not change — that is the whole adjective pattern from the chapter that taught it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മുണ്ട് (muṇṭŭ) ends in the breathed half-u, so ആണ് lands straight on it: മുണ്ടാണ്, nothing slid in — the same join പാട്ട് takes."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So the only new thing here is the word itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "muṇṭŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *muṇṭŭ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "itŭ putiya muṇṭāṇŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *itŭ putiya muṇṭāṇŭ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pāṭṭāṇŭ, then muṇṭāṇŭ, and hear the same landing",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pāṭṭāṇŭ*, then *muṇṭāṇŭ*, and hear the same landing]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is a mundu? (മുണ്ട് (muṇṭŭ).) Where does പുതിയ go, and does it change? (In front, and no.) What slides in before ആണ്? (Nothing — മുണ്ടാണ്.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
