          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സാരി — sāri — a sari."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇത് പഴയ സാരിയാണ്. — itŭ paḻaya sāriyāṇŭ — \"This is an old sari.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two garments, two different landings. മുണ്ട് (muṇṭŭ) ends in the half-u and takes ആണ് straight on. സാരി (sāri) ends in ഇ, and you know what ഇ does:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "word",
                "joined to ആണ്"
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "word: മുണ്ട് (muṇṭŭ). joined to ആണ്: മുണ്ടാണ് (muṇṭāṇŭ).",
                "word: സാരി. joined to ആണ്: സാരിയാണ് (sāriyāṇŭ)."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The യ in സാരിയാണ് is the one കളി and ഭംഗി take, for the reason you were given then: ഇ calls for it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പഴയ behaves as പുതിയ did — in front, unchanged."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
