        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: two endings, and an adjective that never moves",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four things to wear, and between them only two endings:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "ends in",
                "word",
                "joined to ആണ്"
              ],
              "columns": 3,
              "rowCount": 4,
              "utterances": [
                "ends in: half-u. word: മുണ്ട് (muṇṭŭ). joined to ആണ്: മുണ്ടാണ് (muṇṭāṇŭ).",
                "ends in: half-u. word: ചെരുപ്പ് (ceruppŭ). joined to ആണ്: ചെരുപ്പാണ് (ceruppāṇŭ).",
                "ends in: ഇ. word: സാരി. joined to ആണ്: സാരിയാണ് (sāriyāṇŭ).",
                "ends in: ഇ. word: തൊപ്പി. joined to ആണ്: തൊപ്പിയാണ് (toppiyāṇŭ)."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neither join was new, and neither is recent. എന്താണ് has taken the half-u since the book's first question, and കുട്ടി has taken the യ since ഇത് എന്റെ കുട്ടിയാണ് — long before പാട്ട്, കളി or ഭംഗി, which are only the latest words to use them. This chapter spent all four of its words on things, and none on grammar."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇത് പുതിയ മുണ്ടാണ്. — itŭ putiya muṇṭāṇŭ — this is a new mundu. ഇത് പഴയ സാരിയാണ്. — itŭ paḻaya sāriyāṇŭ — this is an old sari."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പുതിയ and പഴയ sit in front and do not change — the same shape they had in the chapter that taught them, with no ending added for the noun that follows."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And the cloth a മുണ്ട് (muṇṭŭ) is made of is തുണി, which the book gave you long before it gave you anything made from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
